(rodeo/screen width height {smooth false}) "Sets the game's size in pixels; the window scales it by whole numbers with black bars, or smoothly by any amount with :smooth true."
(rodeo/size) "The game's [width height] in pixels."
(rodeo/time) "Seconds of game time since the game started, counted in ticks."
(rodeo/ticks) "How many ticks the game has run."
(rodeo/dt) "Seconds per tick, 1/60 by default."
(rodeo/alpha) "How far the frame being drawn is between the last tick and the next, from 0 to 1, for smooth motion."
(rodeo/held? key) "True while key is held, such as :left, :space or :z, or any key of an action named by rodeo/actions."
(rodeo/pressed? key) "True in the first tick after key, or an action's key, went down."
(rodeo/released? key) "True in the first tick after key, or an action's key, came up."
(rodeo/actions bindings) "Names actions for keys, as a map from each action to a vector of keys, such as jump: [:space :up], so rodeo/held? and friends take :jump."
(rodeo/clear color) "Fills the frame with color before anything else is drawn. Colors are \"#rrggbb\" or \"#rrggbbaa\" strings, [red green blue] or [red green blue alpha] vectors from 0 to 255, or :white, :black, :red, :green, :blue, :yellow or :transparent."
(rodeo/rect rect color {stroke nil layer 0}) "Draws the [x y w h] rect filled with color, or outlined :stroke pixels wide."
(rodeo/circle center radius color {stroke nil layer 0}) "Draws a circle around the [x y] center, filled or outlined :stroke pixels wide."
(rodeo/line from to color {width 1 layer 0}) "Draws a line between two [x y] points."
(rodeo/text text at {color :white size 8 layer 0}) "Writes text with its top-left corner at the [x y] point, :size pixels tall in game pixels."
(rodeo/image path) "Loads the image at path, relative to the game's file, as a map of :id, :width and :height for rodeo/sprite; loading it again gives the same image."
(rodeo/cells image width height) "The [x y w h] cells of a sprite sheet image cut into width by height frames, row by row."
(rodeo/sprite image at {region nil rotation 0 scale 1 origin nil flip-x false flip-y false tint nil flash 0 outline nil layer 0}) "Draws image, or its :region, with its :origin, the top-left corner by default, at the [x y] point; :rotation turns it clockwise in radians around the origin, :scale is a number or [x y], :tint multiplies its colors, :flash from 0 to 1 whitens it and :outline draws a one pixel border in a color."
(rodeo/fade color amount) "Covers the whole frame with color at amount from 0 to 1, for fades."
